    _______________

    @article{author = {Coupez, Thierry},
         title  = {Generation de maillage et adaptation de maillage par
                  optimisation locale},
         journal = {Revue Européenne des Éléments Finis},
         volume  = {9}, number = {4}, pages = {403-423}, year = {2000},
         doi     = {10.1080/12506559.2000.10511454}}
     

    @PhdThesis{author = {Cyril Gruau},
           title =  {Generation de métriques pour adaptation anisotrope
              de maillage, application à la mise en forme des matériaux}, 
              school = {ENSMP}, year = {2004}}
      
    @article{author = "Cyril Gruau and Thierry Coupez",
         title = "3D tetrahedral, unstructured and anisotropic mesh
           generation with adaptation to natural and multidomain metric", 
         journal = "Computer Methods in Applied Mechanics and Engineering",
         volume = "194", number = "48 - 49", pages = "4951 - 4976",
         year = "2005",
         doi = "10.1016/j.cma.2004.11.020"}
    
ANGL===========================================================
    Description :
    ___________

    This procedur is not to be called by the user (see operator TRIA
    and REMA).
    It implements a topological algorithm for anisotropic simplices
    mesh generation ('TRIA') or optimisation ('REMA') due to T.
    Coupez et al. (see bibliography)
    
    Contents :
    _________

      MAIL1 : output mesh (MAILLAGE type)

      METR1 : if keyword 'IPOL' is given, METR1 (CHPOINT type) is
              the metric interpolated on the output mesh MAIL1

      MAIL2 : boundary of the output mesh (MAILLAGE type)

      MAIL3 : mesh to be optimized (MAILLAGE type)

      MAIL4 : part of MAIL3's boundary that the algorithm should leave
              untouched (by default it can add or substract nodes on the
              planar parts of MAIL3's boundary)

      METR2 : object of type FLOTTANT or CHPOINT               
              If METR1 is of type FLOTTANT, it is a wanted edge size
              (density)
              If METR1 is of type CHPOINT, It is the inverse of the
              wanted metric field (unit : length^-2)

      TAB1  : optional data of TABLE type the indices of which are
              input or output parameters of the meshing algorithm
              Input :
              TAB1 . 'debug' = 0..2 ; (default value 0)
                   Debug verbosity level
              TAB1 . 'graph' = faux..vrai ; (default value faux)
                   Graphical output
              TAB1 . 'id_cas' = MOT1 ;
                   Character string identifier
              TAB1 . 'max_iter' = ENTI1 ; (default value 100)
                   Maximum iteration number for the algorithm
              TAB1 . 'precrel_volume' = FLOT1 ; (default 1.D-11)
                   Relative precision below which an element
                   is considered flat
              TAB1 . 'precrel_qualite' = FLOT1 ; (default 1.D-2)
                   Relative precision below which two elements are
                   considered to have the same quality
              TAB1 . 'verif' = 0..2 ; (default 0)
                   Verification level (debugging) in operator OPTO
              TAB1 . 'impr_segadj' = 0..1 ; (default 0)
                   Verbosity level (debugging) in memory
                   reallocation (OPTO)
              Output :
              TAB1 . 'curtopo' = MAIL1 ;
                   Current mesh
              TAB1 . 'dvol' = FLOT1 ;
                   Difference between the current mesh volume and the
                   desired volume
              TAB1 . 'nnul' = ENTI1 ;
                   Number of flat elements in the current mesh
              TAB1 . 'miq' = FLOT1 ;
                   Minimum quality (cf. operator INDI) of the current
                   mesh elements
              TAB1 . 'moq' = FLOT1 ;
                   Mean quality of the current mesh elements
              TAB1 . 'maq' = FLOT1 ;
                   Maximum quality of the current mesh elements


    Remarks :
    _________
    
     1) If the metric field is isotropic, its component name is 'G'.
        If the metric field is anisotropic, its component names are:
        G11, G21, G22, (G31, G32, G33 in 3D)

     2) If keyword 'AJNO' (default) is given, the meshing algorithm
        can create new nodes.
        If keyword 'NOAJ' is given, the meshing algorithm doesn't
        create new nodes.


